# Required, not a shortcut — see the "Dependency resolution" section of README.md.
#
# react-native-reanimated 4.7 hard-requires react-native-worklets@0.13.x:
#   peer react-native-worklets: "0.13.x"
#
# expo-modules-core@57.0.20 declares a stale *optional* peer that predates 0.13:
#   peerOptional react-native-worklets: "^0.7.4 || ^0.8.0 || ^0.9.0 || ^0.10.0"
#
# Those two ranges do not intersect, and there is no version of worklets that
# satisfies both: downgrading to 0.10.x breaks Reanimated 4.7 outright. The
# conflict is cosmetic — expo-modules-core only *optionally* peers on worklets
# for its own JSI integration, so 0.13 costs it nothing — but strict resolution
# still refuses, which leaves the lockfile unreproducible and `npm ci` broken.
#
# Recording the flag in the repo makes a fresh clone install the same tree the
# tests were written against, instead of failing with ERESOLVE.
legacy-peer-deps=true
